#!/bin/bash
# Codex comparison arm for the scene pilot. Launch with stdin closed.
cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tio-Documents-GitHub-hermes/eb956062-1d65-4cdb-91a7-e16c0bd73b2d/scratchpad/t228v2 || exit 1
exec codex exec --json --skip-git-repo-check --sandbox workspace-write --color never \
  -o out/codex-arm-final.md \
  "You are the comparison arm of a two-model experiment. Gemma 4 E2B on the cluster just did this exact task; you now do the identical task so the owner can separate model quality from grounding quality. THE TASK, per item: items/items.jsonl holds 16 records with fields id, band, prompt. Each prompt is a complete, self-contained contract: it embeds the figure's written description, the Hermes tool rows Gemma was given, a coordinate-free scene-JSON schema, and one worked example. For each item, produce ONE scene JSON obeying that contract exactly. RULES. (1) Work the 16 items independently; never reuse content across items. (2) You have the hermes MCP tools live — the same system the embedded rows came from. You MAY make additional hermes calls where the embedded rows feel thin or wrong; when you do, write what you called and what you used to out/codex-arm/mcp_log/ITEMID.txt. Your judgment about where the rows were insufficient is half the experiment: the owner wants to know how much of round one's mediocrity was the small model and how much was the Prolog grounding. (3) Validate each draft locally before accepting it: read gate_scene.py to learn its interface (or validate via python3 -c with scene_schema.validate); on a refusal, revise ONCE — two tries total, matching Gemma's retry budget. (4) Write the final raw JSON (json only, no fences) to out/codex-arm/raw/ITEMID.txt. (5) Write out/codex-arm/report.md: one line per item (valid, tries, extra MCP calls yes/no, one-phrase self-assessment) followed by a short section titled 'Where the grounding was the limit' listing, per item where it applies, what the embedded rows lacked or misstated — cite the row, not a vibe. (6) Write nothing outside out/codex-arm/. No git operations. End your report with ARM_COMPLETE or ARM_PARTIAL and a count of valid items." \
  > out/codex-arm-events.ndjson 2>&1
